    "question": "A large number $n$ of identical liquid droplets of radius $r$, density $\\rho$, and specific heat capacity $s$ coalesce to form a single spherical drop of radius $R$. Assuming all the liberated surface energy is converted entirely into internal thermal energy of the resulting drop, the rise in temperature $\\Delta\\theta$ of the drop is: (Surface tension $= T$, mechanical equivalent of heat $= J$)",
